Recognise GSMA RSP certificate policies

mbedTLS enforces certificatePolicies by refusing to parse any certificate whose
policy extension is marked critical and names a policy it does not itself know.
Only anyPolicy is known, so every GSMA RSP certificate issued under the arc
2.23.146.1.2.1 fails to parse with MBEDTLS_ERR_X509_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE.

That is fatal for an ES9+ client on this platform. The GSMA CI roots carry
2.23.146.1.2.1.0 marked critical, and an SM-DP+ may send its issuing root inside
its own TLS chain -- two of the three live Consumer servers this project has
measured do. The peer chain is parsed by the SSL layer before any authmode is
consulted, so such a server cannot be reached at all: not with verification, and
not with verification disabled either.

mbedtls_x509_crt_parse_der_with_ext_cb() is the sanctioned escape for a policy
the application understands, but it is reachable only where the application does
the parsing, and the peer chain is parsed inside the handshake.

So this build recognises the one policy arc it does in fact understand. The
change is deliberately narrower than MBEDTLS_X509_ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED_CRITICAL_-
EXTENSION: an unknown critical extension stays fatal, an unknown critical policy
outside the GSMA RSP arc stays fatal, and nothing about validation changes. The
certificate is still verified normally afterwards; all that is added is the
ability to read it.

This patch applies to a copy of mbedTLS built into apn-autoconfig-esim's own
ES9+ client and linked statically. The system TLS library is not touched and no
other package's behaviour changes.

--- a/library/x509_crt.c
+++ b/library/x509_crt.c
@@ -736,6 +736,31 @@
  * NOTE: we only parse and use anyPolicy without qualifiers at this point
  * as defined in RFC 5280.
  */
+/*
+ * GSMA RSP certificate policies: joint-iso-itu-t(2) international-
+ * organizations(23) gsma(146) rsp(1) certificate-policies(2) v2(1), which
+ * encodes as 67 81 12 01 02 01 followed by the individual policy arc. The CI
+ * roots use ...1.0 and SM-DP+ leaves ...1.3; the whole arc is matched so a
+ * later policy in the same tree does not reintroduce the parse failure.
+ */
+#define X509_GSMA_RSP_POLICY_PREFIX "\x67\x81\x12\x01\x02\x01"
+#define X509_GSMA_RSP_POLICY_PREFIX_LEN 6
+
+static int x509_policy_is_understood(const mbedtls_x509_buf *policy_oid)
+{
+    if (MBEDTLS_OID_CMP(MBEDTLS_OID_ANY_POLICY, policy_oid) == 0) {
+        return 1;
+    }
+
+    if (policy_oid->len > X509_GSMA_RSP_POLICY_PREFIX_LEN &&
+        memcmp(policy_oid->p, X509_GSMA_RSP_POLICY_PREFIX,
+               X509_GSMA_RSP_POLICY_PREFIX_LEN) == 0) {
+        return 1;
+    }
+
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static int x509_get_certificate_policies(unsigned char **p,
                                          const unsigned char *end,
                                          mbedtls_x509_sequence *certificate_policies)
@@ -789,9 +814,10 @@
         policy_oid.p = *p;
 
         /*
-         * Only AnyPolicy is currently supported when enforcing policy.
+         * anyPolicy, and the GSMA RSP arc this build exists to read, are
+         * understood when enforcing policy.
          */
-        if (MBEDTLS_OID_CMP(MBEDTLS_OID_ANY_POLICY, &policy_oid) != 0) {
+        if (!x509_policy_is_understood(&policy_oid)) {
             /*
              * Set the parsing return code but continue parsing, in case this
              * extension is critical.
